{"name":"Rocket Metallic","hex":"#8a7f80","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rocket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A projectile.\nA cylindrical projectile that can be fired to a great height through combustion,  a type of firework of this form, typically exploding with light and colour; a skyrocket. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\nA blunt lance head used in jousting.\nA long vehicle or craft propelled by a rocket engine; a missile or rocket-propelled spacecraft. \n\nAn engine operating similarly to the pyrotechnic, generating thrust by the expulsion of hot gases; a rocket engine.","A cylindrical projectile that can be fired to a great height through combustion,  a type of firework of this form, typically exploding with light and colour; a skyrocket. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To accelerate swiftly and powerfully.","To fly vertically."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocket"},{"term":"metallic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or characteristic of metal.","Made of or containing metal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metallic color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metallic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rocket","blocks":[{"text":"A rocket is an elongated flying vehicle that uses a rocket engine to accelerate without using any surrounding air. A rocket engine produces thrust by reaction to exhaust expelled at high speed. Unlike jet engines, rockets are fuelled entirely by propellant which they carry, without the need for oxygen from air; consequently a rocket can fly in the vacuum of space, and indeed rocket engines operate more efficiently outside the atmosphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Soyuz_TMA-9_launch.jpg/330px-Soyuz_TMA-9_launch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket","w